1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:09,214
ChatGPT Wallet: before, you'd stop, type your card; now 1 scan, it pays, never seeing your 3 numbers, but how, why, in 60 seconds?

2
00:00:09,714 --> 00:00:11,098
Here's how, in one errand:

3
00:00:11,098 --> 00:00:12,687
you send a helper to the shop.

4
00:00:12,987 --> 00:00:15,751
Before, ChatGPT's agent stopped at checkout.

5
00:00:16,051 --> 00:00:18,666
You took over its browser, typed your real card,

6
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:20,588
and the shop got all three numbers.

7
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:22,722
Now, since November 13,

8
00:00:22,722 --> 00:00:24,100
your dot carries a wallet.

9
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,264
At checkout it shows you the items,

10
00:00:26,264 --> 00:00:27,507
the total and the card.

11
00:00:27,807 --> 00:00:30,085
You approve with Face ID or a fingerprint.

12
00:00:30,385 --> 00:00:32,796
Then the card network hands over a stand-in:

13
00:00:32,796 --> 00:00:34,457
its own number, code and date.

14
00:00:34,957 --> 00:00:37,201
The shop charges the stand-in; the bill

15
00:00:37,201 --> 00:00:39,557
lands on your real card, rewards and all.

16
00:00:39,857 --> 00:00:41,534
Your agent never sees your card,

17
00:00:41,534 --> 00:00:42,907
and neither does the shop.

18
00:00:43,407 --> 00:00:45,809
How? One scan, then a stand-in card.

19
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:47,663
Why? Your three numbers

20
00:00:47,663 --> 00:00:48,679
stay out of the errand.

21
00:00:48,979 --> 00:00:51,080
For now, only Pro users in America,

22
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,772
and some shops may block it.

23
00:00:53,072 --> 00:00:54,877
Your helper still runs the errand;

24
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:56,579
it just never holds your wallet.

25
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:58,481
Subscribe for the next one.
